  "description": "<p>The Fedora repository can act like a registry of services <br/>\nvia BDef objects. This could be done by having the <br/>\nBDef objects contain a datastream that is WSDL that <br/>\nbinds to a Fedora repository as the proxy for end-point <br/>\nservice. When Fedora repositories are federated, this <br/>\ncan act like a UDDI repository, but maybe simpler.<br/>\nDate: 2005-03-24 11:31<br/>\nSender: payette<br/>\nLogged In: YES <br/>\nuser_id=128<br/>\nClever notion to have BDef's with fedora dissemination <br/>\nbindings (template with pids as variable).  Look at this <br/>\nin context of federation or dynamic disseminations.<br/>\nDate: 2004-09-07 11:36<br/>\nSender: payette<br/>\nLogged In: YES <br/>\nuser_id=128<br/>\nAlso, can we implement a UDDI 2.0 interface over Fedora to <br/>\nmake it work as if it were a UDDI registry?</p>",
